cerberus-client (cssh) for Debian
=================================

Set your signing endpoint in /etc/profile.d/cerberus-env.sh (or export
CERBERUS_URL), then open a new login shell so the cssh function is defined. For
OIDC (no Kerberos) login, set CSSH_AUTH=oidc and the CSSH_OIDC_* values there.

Note: /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh is program code, not site config, and it is a
symlink to /usr/lib/cerberus/cssh.sh. Every upgrade replaces that script, so
fixes always apply — including on hosts where an admin had edited the old file.
Up to 0.14.0 the path was a regular file and therefore a dpkg conffile; if you
had modified it, the upgrade preserves your copy as
/etc/profile.d/cssh.sh.dpkg-bak for reference, and it no longer takes effect.
Put site config in cerberus-env.sh, which stays a conffile: your edits there
survive upgrades. See cssh.md in this directory.

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>
